From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darwin-vm contributors <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/xnuboot: select XNU graphics console

A valid Boot_Video framebuffer is not enough by itself. XNU's platform
expert checks v_display and only initializes kPEGraphicsMode when it equals
the bootloader GRAPHICS_MODE value. Select that mode so the early video
console actually renders into the framebuffer.
---
 hw/arm/xnuboot_sptm.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/xnuboot_sptm.c b/hw/arm/xnuboot_sptm.c
--- a/hw/arm/xnuboot_sptm.c
+++ b/hw/arm/xnuboot_sptm.c
@@ -91,11 +91,11 @@ static void configure_boot_video(boot_args *args,
 
     /*
      * XNU treats bit 0 of v_baseAddr as "this is a physical address" and
-     * maps the framebuffer itself.  Keep v_display=0 for the first milestone
-     * so PE_create_console() selects the built-in text console.
+     * maps the framebuffer itself. XNU's bootloader GRAPHICS_MODE value is 1;
+     * PE_create_console() uses it to select kPEGraphicsMode.
      */
     args->Video.v_baseAddr = info->fb_base | 1;
-    args->Video.v_display = 0;
+    args->Video.v_display = 1;
     args->Video.v_rowBytes = DARWIN_BOOT_FB_ROW_BYTES;
     args->Video.v_width = DARWIN_BOOT_FB_WIDTH;
     args->Video.v_height = DARWIN_BOOT_FB_HEIGHT;
